course: dictionary
lesson: 6034
title: Melon: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A melon is a big, round or oval fruit with a hard skin and a sweet, juicy inside full of seeds. Watermelon, cantaloupe and honeydew are all kinds of melon. «He packs bananas, sugar-cane and melons» shows melons being bought and carried like other fruit.
explain: Context tells you which meaning a word has. In «Going home he pulled fruit down from trees», the word fruit points to the food meaning of melon. Before you choose a meaning, read the sentence around the word and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: Some words have a special meaning in science. «A beluga whale can change the shape of its melon to aim its clicks» uses melon in a different way. Here it means the rounded part of the whale's forehead, not a fruit at all. The sentence around it makes this clear.
fact: A melon is a fruit with a hard skin and sweet, juicy inside.
fact: Watermelon, cantaloupe and honeydew are all kinds of melon.
fact: Melons grow on vines and are mostly water.
fact: In «a beluga can change the shape of its melon», melon means the rounded part of a whale's forehead.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the sentence around it tells you which one to use.
exercise: Which of these is a kind of melon? | Banana | Carrot | *Honeydew | Sugar-cane
exercise: In «He packs bananas, sugar-cane and melons», what is a melon? | *A fruit that can be counted and sold | A lamp for the kitchen | A tool for cutting wood | A kind of cloud
exercise: In «a beluga can change the shape of its melon to aim its clicks», what is the melon? | A bowl of fruit | A fin on its back | The whale's tail | *The rounded part of the whale's forehead
test: A melon grows on a... | Bush | Rock | *Vine | Tree
test: Which of these is NOT a kind of melon? | *Banana | Honeydew | Watermelon | Cantaloupe
exam: What is the best meaning of melon in «We cut the melon into equal slices for the picnic»? | *A fruit with a hard skin and sweet, juicy inside | A kind of pudding | A picnic blanket | A kitchen knife
